+
+### REQ-PHASE4-4424: ARC-AGI-3 Single Solved-Game Lookahead-Fidelity Decomposition Exp4424
+**Description:** The system SHALL run Exp 4424 as an offline, no-leaderboard checkpoint over exactly one solved high-headroom game chosen from the current `ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml` prior bests. It MUST target the next level beyond that prior best, decompose the lookahead-fidelity blocker by running a K-step world-model rollout against the offline environment, identify the concrete mismatched transition(s), add executable per-mechanic unit tests that cite `REQ-PHASE4-4424` or `SCENARIO-PHASE4-4424`, and apply only targeted engine patches that make those tests pass. A new level SHALL count only when `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()` or an injected equivalent proves the target level beyond the prior best. The terminal artifact `results/experiment_4424_deeper_solved_game.json` MUST include bare top-level fields `offline_reproduced`, `reproduced_levels`, `verifier_is_oracle=true`, and `honest_verdict`, plus per-mechanic test rows whose pass/fail status is reported separately from the solve claim. Honest partials MUST include the now-passing per-mechanic transition test(s) and a residual failing-mechanic gap class rather than converting fidelity repair into a solve.
